 "asked_at": "2026-10-17T19:07+08:00",
 "answer": "Yes, the haze is bad in Singapore today. Air quality remains in the **unhealthy** range across the island, continuing a prolonged stretch of poor air quality driven by smoke drifting from fires in Kalimantan and Sumatra, Indonesia. \n\n* **PSI Levels:** The 24-hour Pollutant Standards Index (PSI) ranges across regions from roughly **135 to 185**, which falls firmly into the **Unhealthy** band. (This is a slight dip from yesterday's peak, which hit \"Very Unhealthy\" levels in parts of the island).\n* **PM2.5 Concentrations:** Hourly PM2.5 readings have entered the **high** range in several regions (such as the west, central, south, and east), meaning there are elevated levels of fine particles right now.\n\n**Advisories:**\n* **General Public:** Should avoid prolonged or strenuous outdoor physical exertion.\n* **Elderly, pregnant women, children, and those with chronic heart or lung conditions:** Advised to minimize or avoid outdoor activities altogether. \n\nBecause haze conditions can fluctuate quickly depending on the wind and weather, it is recommended to check real-time updates on the **myENV app** or the National Environment Agency (NEA) haze site (`www.haze.gov.sg`) before heading out.",
